WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.964
The lasting message is twofold.

00:00:04.044 --> 00:00:08.008
Practically,

00:00:08.088 --> 00:00:12.052
explanation generation can be added to a
state-of-the-art VQA backbone with almost no loss in answer accuracy,

00:00:12.132 --> 00:00:16.096
giving users a human-readable reason alongside each
answer.

00:00:16.176 --> 00:00:20.140
But methodologically,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.184
the paper shows through concrete examples that
string-matching metrics like BLEU and ROUGE

00:00:24.264 --> 00:00:28.228
can reward a wrong explanation and penalize a valid one,

00:00:28.308 --> 00:00:32.272
so they are unreliable for this task.

00:00:32.352 --> 00:00:36.316
The authors therefore argue that the real
bottleneck for explainable VQA is not the generator but the evaluation,

00:00:36.396 --> 00:00:40.360
and they urge the community to develop proper
reasoning-aware metrics for judging explanations.
